  :seon.task/plan "Goal: one standard every Seon proc follows, written once in docs/flow.md (stays at most 110 lines, shorter), each pattern with a small runnable example that is a test, so it stays true; plus an inventory of what should be a Flow proc and is not, each filed as a task for its owner. Root approved 2026-11-13; context indexes the examples so an agent touching a pattern is shown them. What exists: docs/flow.md (110 lines), web-research/flow-source.md (upstream against Jolt, line by line), deps' Flow gaps A-E, and port names in use (:to-api x7, :in x5, :main x4, fifteen one-offs). Standard: (1) naming: in-ports named for what arrives, out-ports :to-<pid> when feeding one proc else named for what leaves, replies on the asker's :answers, one key for a reply address and :seon.bound/bound for a message's bound; (2) lifecycle: init takes nothing from outside but in-ports/out-ports, pause and resume idempotent, stop releases everything and answers every open request :stopped, a transition's throw is reported with its command, pause leaves in-flight messages in buffers [M]; (3) patterns each with an example: request/reply by rid, completion as close, fan-out, fan-in, back-pressure, pipelines (lift1->step), deadlines as messages, effects; (4) not allowed: atom as proc state, thread outside declared edges, blocking take in a step, poll, clock read, FIFO-position answers. Measured at the REPL on Jolt, n at most 4 [M]: rid replies match; a throwing step does not stop the proc; an output to a missing coord gives no error, only ::flow/undeliverable on the report chan; a closed in-port yields one nil in order; a deadline via a/timeout onto the own in-port arrives as a message; an open request at stop is not answered by Flow, it is the owner's job. Examples: test/seon/flow_patterns_test.clj, one deftest per pattern, 15-25 lines, ~8 tests ~5M ticks, red first under a mutation. Inventory tasks: the test child's link (second EDN codec, a guard turning undecodable into a value, a pid stamped in the decoder) is built first after the standard: one codec jfasl, an unreadable value as the link's typed error, fan-in knowing its senders; the agent's state and link atoms (agent.clj:36, 41); await-reply's promise table (agent.clj:235); the 7888 server's accept thread (server.clj:633); tree-runs atom (system.clj:2126); server's index-now atom (server.clj:69). Left alone: fork_server loop, fx read-lines! thread, intr and uncaught atoms (edges), caches (values kept by input)."
